# TEMPLATE — delete this block when instantiating.
#
#     Copy to <repo>/justfile. Written once at project bootstrap by
#     /project-init, then owned by the human. No skill edits it afterwards,
#     except to append a `verify` recipe when one is missing.
#
#     `verify` is the contract. /implement will not call a task done until it
#     exits zero, so it has to run everything CI runs. Derive the body from the
#     repo's actual CI workflow and existing scripts — not from a guess about
#     the stack. A stack guess produces a plausible recipe that misses the two
#     checks this particular repo actually cares about.
#
#     Compose, never duplicate. Give each check its own recipe and let `verify`
#     depend on them. A command written in two places drifts.
#
#     The recipe names below are placeholders too. Use whatever this repo calls
#     these things, and add or drop rows freely — three is not a target.
#
#     UPGRADE, once there are more than a couple of checks: `just` dependencies
#     are fail-fast, so the first broken check hides every one after it.
#     Replace the body with a bash block that runs all of them, collects the
#     failures and prints one summary at the end. One run then tells the whole
#     story instead of one failure per run.
#
#     Body placeholders after this block is deleted: <lint>, <types>, <test>,
#     their three <...-command> lines, and the three <what this checks> docs.

default:
    @just --list --unsorted

# Run every check. THE entrypoint after implementing a feature.
verify: <lint> <types> <test>

# <what this checks>
<lint>:
    <lint-command>

# <what this checks>
<types>:
    <types-command>

# <what this checks>
<test>:
    <test-command>
